' Where a detail screen's rows start, and the "Spotlight" backdrop every
' detail page shares with the Spotlight list page (owner, 2026-11-11): the
' picture full-bleed across the right ~70% of the screen, flush top-right, its
' left part fading into the page under the text column and its lower part
' fading into the page under the rows, which sit over that faded part. The
' fades are flat overlays in the page colour (spotlight_fade_left.png /
' spotlight_fade_bottom.png), not a MaskGroup: cheaper on low-end Rokus, and
' they fade the hero trailer the same way they fade the still. Pure functions
' only, so tests/DetailLayoutTests.brs can run them off-device.
namespace DetailLayout

    ' The y the RowList (Seasons / Episodes / Cast) starts at.
    function rowsTop(itemType as dynamic) as integer
        if itemType = "Season" then return 480
        return 734
    end function

    ' The backdrop's region: { x, w, h } in screen pixels, 16:9, flush with
    ' the top-right corner.
    function spotlight() as object
        return { x: 560, w: 1360, h: 765 }
    end function

    ' The two fades over a picture drawn in `r` ({ x, w, h }, flush top-
    ' right): the left one over its left 720/1360 (opaque page at the edge,
    ' clear at the end), the bottom one over its lower 400/765 (clear at the
    ' top, opaque page at the bottom). Scaled with it, so a smaller
    ' picture (a wide banner, a scope trailer) fades the same way.
    function fades(r as object) as object
        lw = Int(r.w * 720 / 1360 + 0.5)
        bh = Int(r.h * 400 / 765 + 0.5)
        return { left: { x: r.x, y: 0, w: lw, h: r.h }, bottom: { x: r.x, y: r.h - bh, w: r.w, h: bh } }
    end function

    ' Where a picture of `aspect` (width / height) is drawn. A backdrop (and
    ' anything not much wider than 16:9) is zoomed to fill the whole region;
    ' wider art -- a YouTube channel's banner -- is fitted, flush top-right,
    ' since zooming a 5:1 banner to the region's height would show a slice of
    ' it blown up several times.
    function artBox(aspect as dynamic) as object
        r = spotlight()
        if aspect = invalid or aspect <= 0 or aspect <= 2.1 then return r
        return trailerBox(r.w, r.h, aspect)
    end function

    ' The hero trailer's own rectangle: its aspect (16:9 when unknown) fitted
    ' into the region, flush with the top-right corner. Not the still
    ' backdrop's rectangle: a trailer played inside a box of another shape
    ' letterboxes, and its black bars' inner edges are hard lines the fades
    ' never reach (#257). { x, w, h } in screen pixels.
    function trailerBox(regionW as integer, regionH as integer, aspect as dynamic) as object
        a = 16.0 / 9.0
        if aspect <> invalid and aspect > 0 then a = aspect
        w = regionW
        h = Int(w / a + 0.5)
        if h > regionH
            h = regionH
            w = Int(h * a + 0.5)
        end if
        return { x: 1920 - w, w: w, h: h }
    end function

end namespace
